---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const html = "<main id=\"main\"><section class=\"page page-standalone\" id=\"privacy\" aria-labelledby=\"h-pp\">\n  <div class=\"page-inner\">\n    <p class=\"eyebrow\">Legal</p>\n    <h1 id=\"h-pp\">Privacy policy</h1>\n    <p class=\"updated\">Last updated: 26 November 2026</p>\n    <p>This policy explains what personal data renderly.art collects, why, and your rights under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and Spanish Organic Law 3/2018 (LOPDGDD).</p>\n    <h2>1. Data controller</h2>\n    <p>Marta Camps Fuster (Renderly Studio) · NIF 43457339N · 08100 Mollet del Vallès (Barcelona), Spain · hello@renderly.art</p>\n    <h2>2. What we collect and why</h2>\n    <table>\n      <thead><tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Data</th><th>Legal basis</th><th>How long</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td>Launch list and newsletter</td><td>Email address, signup date, confirmation status</td><td>Your consent (Art. 6.1.a GDPR), given with the checkbox and email confirmation</td><td>Until you unsubscribe</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Answering custom work enquiries</td><td>Name, email, project details you send</td><td>Steps at your request before a contract (Art. 6.1.b GDPR)</td><td>12 months after the last contact, or the legal period if a contract follows</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Site statistics</td><td>Anonymous, aggregated visit data. No cookies, no IP stored</td><td>Legitimate interest in knowing how the site is used (Art. 6.1.f GDPR)</td><td>Aggregated only</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n    <p>We do not sell your data, use it for profiling or send it to advertisers.</p>\n    <h2>3. Who processes it for us</h2>\n    <table>\n      <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Role</th><th>Location / safeguards</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n                        <tr><td>Google (Gmail)</td><td>Email inbox for hello@renderly.art</td><td>EU–US Data Privacy Framework</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Cloudflare</td><td>DNS, security and cookieless analytics</td><td>EU–US Data Privacy Framework</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>GitHub (Microsoft)</td><td>Hosts the website files</td><td>EU–US Data Privacy Framework</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n    <p>When you buy on Fab, Unity Asset Store or Gumroad, that marketplace is responsible for your purchase data under its own privacy policy.</p>\n    <h2>4. Your rights</h2>\n    <p>You can ask to access, correct or delete your data, restrict or object to its use, receive it in a portable format, and withdraw your consent at any time. Every email has an unsubscribe link. Write to hello@renderly.art; we answer within one month.</p>\n    <p>If you think your data has been mishandled, you can complain to the Spanish Data Protection Agency (<a href=\"https://www.aepd.es\" rel=\"noopener\">aepd.es</a>).</p>\n    <h2>5. Age</h2>\n    <p>The newsletter is for people aged 14 or over, the age of digital consent in Spain.</p>\n    <h2>6. Changes</h2>\n    <p>If this policy changes, the date above will change. Significant changes will be announced to the list.</p>\n  </div>\n</section></main>";
---
<Base title="Privacy policy · Renderly Studio" description="How renderly.art handles personal data." path="/privacy">
<Fragment set:html={html} />
</Base>
